    {
      "lang": "en",
      "label": "#726: keep a table per level, then merge a child (different counting rules)",
      "href": "../726/#step2",
      "resolved": "http://127.0.0.1:18770/leetcode/726/#step2",
      "keyboard": "Enter",
      "width": 320,
      "heading": "03 · Keep counts at each level",
      "destinationText": "03 · Keep counts at each levelHow do we separate inside from outside? A dictionary is a name-to-count table. A stack keeps these tables in order; the last table belongs to the innermost group. In Mg(OH)2, reading Mg gives {Mg:1}. At (, keep it and open an empty table. After OH, the outer table is {Mg:1} and the inner table is {O:1,H:1}.At )2, remove the inner table. Compute O: 0 + 1×2 = 2 and H: 0 + 1×2 = 2, then add them to the parent; Mg:1 stays unchanged. With more nesting, this merged table becomes part of its enclosing group. In K4(ON(SO3)2)2, the inner group contributes O:6,S:2. Add the existing O:1,N:1, then multiply by 2: O:14,S:4,N:2. K remains 4.These operations give an invariant, a fact preserved after each complete operation: each table counts exactly the completed units at its own level. It excludes unfinished child groups and any multiplier outside that level. Atoms add only to the last table; opening leaves the parent untouched; closing multiplies each child entry once before merging. Thus the parent prefix is never multiplied accidentally. Valid input ends with one base table containing all atoms. Sorting changes only output order.Try this: keep the formula fixed and advance one operation. Compare the before and after columns. At a close, inspect which counts multiply and which stay unchanged. Back restores the complete state. Choosing another example restarts this trace; the prediction is independent.Teaching simulation, not Python execution in the browser. Each frame completes an atom with its count, an opening parenthesis, or a closing parenthesis with its multiplier. All operations are retained. Tables run from outermost to innermost; the consumed prefix is not the final output.Formula (changing restarts)Mg(OH)2H2OK4(ON(SO3)2)2He(H2O)2(OH)3Be12H2((H)2O)3H← Previous operationNext operation →Reset traceGo to final resultOperation 0/6 · consumed characters 0/7Consumed: (none)Nothing consumed; the base table is empty.Before · outer → innerLevel 0Empty tableAfter · outer → innerLevel 0Empty tableFinal output: not emitted yetCompleted operation history",
      "destinationSha256": "7701953c73ae0f2b6e3574a4ecbc50a0041b182e75d18a7f585f5851621ccd01"
